  "mapping_lifecycle": {
    "submission_drain": "Existing ZornGen7HostRing26::quiesceKernelIo waits selected direct submission fences, checks the direct ring idle, and rejects outstanding work from nonselected process clients before the public BO map/free path enters the SMMU gate.",
    "runtime_routes": "The host runtime VM and each process VM now carry mandatory haltForTableUpdate and releaseAfterTableUpdate callbacks backed by the retained ZornGen7SmmuDomain26 and ZornGen7RegisterMaps26 owners.",
    "map": "Rejects while the VM has unretired submission resources; retains/publishes the BO, requests the bounded GMU-idle and ordered GBIF client/arbitration halt with ACKs, performs the live context batch update including translation synchronization, revalidates owner routes, then releases GBIF before publishing the handle.",
    "unmap": "Keeps the existing outstanding-resource refusal; after the caller drains tracked work, performs the same verified GBIF halt around live unmap and TLBSYNC, revalidates, and releases before retiring the backing reference.",
    "failure": "A table, halt, or release error follows the existing VM fail path and faults the owned stream. Uncertain GBIF leases are terminal, mapped backing remains retained/quarantined, and the domain is stopped; no reset/retry is synthesized.",
    "scope": "These callbacks close the live Direct VM table-update lifecycle in the candidate. They do not create the missing OS/board startup authority provider or independently prove all producer/scheduler ownership."
  },
